olicy-success gains.', `finding`: 'Physical tables compare reward accuracy, inference time and query counts; these are feedback-system outcomes, not physical policy-success gains.', `evaluation`: 'Section 4.4 and Table 4; physical evaluation is distinct from the simulated training environments in Appendix C.1.', `participants`: '', `extraSupport`: 'Task description and observed robot workspace.', `limitations`: 'Do not transfer simulated RL claims to the real robot. The phrase training-free refers to reward generation without task-training the VLM; the robot policy is still trained with RL in simulation.', `scopeReason`: 'The physical experiment measures reward accuracy and computation, without demonstrating a physical RL policy update.', `uncertainties`: ['Physical task names are not fully specified in the passages retained for this targeted review; do not invent them. No hardware policy update is evidenced in the inspected methods and experiments.']});
