d online adaptation and is excluded from this row.', `result`: 'Before online adaptation, the ReWiND-initialized policy averages 12% success over five reported physical evaluation tasks; corresponding VLC initial policy averages 8%.', `finding`: 'Initial mean success 12%; later online adaptation is outside this table.', `evaluation`: '20,000 offline updates; initial physical result in Figure 6/Section 4.2. Evaluation trial denominator and independent training replication are not established.', `participants`: '', `extraSupport`: 'Physical demonstrations: 10 per policy-training task (5 per task for reward learning); task language; frozen pretrained representations; retained success bonus.', `limitations`: 'Initial-stage performance/generalization evidence is limited. It is not an independent experiment proving a large offline benefit, nor evidence of first-category online hardware learning. The teacher is a learned head over FM features rather than a general VLM prompted as evaluator.', `scopeReason`: 'A new domain-specific actor is learned through offline IQL with learned model rewards before any online adaptation. This is eligible first-category policy learning; it is a stage of ReWiND, not another independent study.', `uncertainties`: ['C.1 describes 10 demonstrations over 20 tasks, while C.2 separately describes 15 reward-model training tasks and 5 evaluation tasks; do not assume all these splits are identical.', 'Physical evaluation trial count and independent training repetitions are not established.', 'The success bonus is described for policy rewards, but its offline-label implementation is not isolated in the inspected experimental prose.']});
